**`LogScreen.tsx` — Multiple analytics computed outside `useMemo`**

```tsx
// Current — recomputes on every render
const summary = buildSummary(logs);
const healthScore = calculateTrainingLogHealthScore(logs);
const readinessTrend = buildReadinessTrend(logs);
const sessionRecommendation = buildSessionRecommendation(logs);
const weeklyLoadRisk = buildWeeklyLoadRisk(logs);
```

```tsx
// Fix — memoize all derived values together
const { summary, healthScore, readinessTrend, sessionRecommendation, weeklyLoadRisk } = useMemo(() => ({
  summary: buildSummary(logs),
  healthScore: calculateTrainingLogHealthScore(logs),
  readinessTrend: buildReadinessTrend(logs),
  sessionRecommendation: buildSessionRecommendation(logs),
  weeklyLoadRisk: buildWeeklyLoadRisk(logs),
}), [logs]);
```

These functions iterate over the `logs` array multiple times — each independently. Memoizing eliminates redundant passes on every state change (filter, sort, search query).

---

**`DashboardScreen.tsx` — Same `logs` array iterated 7+ times**

`buildWeekSummary`, `buildReadinessTrend`, `buildWeeklyLoadRisk`, `getStrengthStatus`, `getEnduranceStatus`, `getRecoveryStatus`, plus `logs.find(...)` called 4 times — all on every render. Apply the same `useMemo` pattern.

---

**`TrainingLogCard.tsx` — Not memoized; re-renders on every list update**

```tsx
// Fix — wrap in React.memo
export default React.memo(function TrainingLogCard({ log, onEdit, onDelete }: Props) {
  ...
});
```

Since it's rendered inside a `FlatList`, every parent state change (search query keystroke, filter toggle) re-renders all visible cards. Combine with stable `onEdit`/`onDelete` callbacks using `useCallback` in `LogScreen`.

```tsx
// LogScreen.tsx
const handleEdit = useCallback((id: number) => router.push(`/edit-log/${id}`), [router]);
const handleDelete = useCallback((log: TrainingLog) => confirmDeleteLog(log), []);
```

---

**`TrainingLogForm.tsx` — `notesWarning` not memoized**

```tsx
// Current
const notesWarning = getNotesQualityWarning(notes);

// Fix
const notesWarning = useMemo(() => getNotesQualityWarning(notes), [notes]);
```

`getNotesQualityWarning` runs string ops on every render. Minor, but it fires on every keystroke across all fields.

---

`buildWeeklyReport` calls 8 separate functions, each iterating `logs`:

```ts
// Current — ~8 separate filter/map passes over logs
const thisWeek = buildWeekSummary(logs, 0);
const summary = buildSummary(logs);
const healthScore = calculateTrainingLogHealthScore(logs);
// ...
const weakLogs = logs.filter((log) => getWeakLogReasons(log).length > 0);
const fatigueWatchLogs = logs.filter((log) => isFatigueWatch(log.readiness));
```

For report generation (a one-shot call), this is acceptable — but `getWeakLogReasons` is called twice per log (once in `calculateTrainingLogHealthScore` inside `trainingLogUtils`, once in the `weakLogs` filter). If `trainingLogUtils` exposes those intermediate results, pass them through rather than recomputing.

---

**`TrainingLogForm.tsx` — `useEffect` syncing `initialValues`**

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  setDate(initialValues.date);
  setCategory(initialValues.category);
  // ...6 setState calls
}, [initialValues]);
```

This triggers 6 synchronous state updates in sequence, causing 6 re-renders. Consolidate into a single state object, or use a `useReducer`:

```tsx
// Simpler fix — single state reset
const [values, setValues] = useState(initialValues);
useEffect(() => { setValues(initialValues); }, [initialValues]);
```

---

